This is not a channel send, and `ManagedServer::stop` genuinely fails on a non-`ESRCH` signal error (opencode/server.rs:158-169: `signal_group(self.pid, libc::SIGTERM)?`), as does `RunningProcess::stop` (claude/process.rs:108-125). After the early return nothing else holds the provider: `runtime` is dropped and the thread is never inserted into `inner.threads`.

crates/fleet-daemon/src/services/agents/manager/tests.rs:363-381
```rust
/// Polls the projection until `predicate` holds, failing the test on timeout.
async fn settle(&self, thread: ThreadId, what: &str, predicate: impl Fn(&ThreadProjection) -> bool) -> ThreadProjection {
    tokio::time::timeout(SETTLE, async { loop {
        let projection = self.projection(thread).await;
        if predicate(&projection) { return projection; }
        tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(5)).await;
    } }).await.unwrap_or_else(|_| panic!("agent thread never reached {what}"))
}
```
`const SETTLE: Duration = Duration::from_secs(5);` (`:32`), 19 call sites of `settle(`, plus an open-coded copy of the same loop at `:1226-1240`. The whole workspace has exactly one `#[tokio::test(start_paused = true)]` (`crates/fleet-daemon/src/machines/link.rs:923`) despite `tokio` `test-util` being a dev-dependency (`crates/fleet-daemon/Cargo.toml:45`).

